  "id": "sleep-spindles",
  "term": "sleep spindles",
  "definition": "Sleep spindles are brief patterns of brain activity during sleep that have been linked to memory-related sleep processes and cognitive abilities. They are thought to help coordinate communication between the hippocampus and neocortex involved in forming memories.",
